NEARS-1334 QA — live HTTP evidence
Server: php artisan serve --host=127.0.0.1 --port=8010 (worktree Admin/, DB multi_food_db, read-only)
Route under test: GET /api/v1/vendor/profile (middleware: vendor.api -> VendorTokenIsValid)

=== AC1: bogus vendorType header, non-empty bearer ===
$ curl -H "Authorization: [REDACTED bearer, garbage value]" -H "vendorType: garbage" http://127.0.0.1:8010/api/v1/vendor/profile
{"errors":[{"code":"auth-001","message":"Unauthorized."}]}
HTTP_STATUS:401
RESULT: PASS — fails closed, matches AC exactly.

=== AC2: owner happy path (seeded auth_token, vendors.id=1) ===
$ curl -H "Authorization: [REDACTED bearer, seeded owner auth_token]" -H "vendorType: owner" http://127.0.0.1:8010/api/v1/vendor/profile
HTTP_STATUS:200
{"id":1,"f_name":"Demo","l_name":"Store", ... "stores":[...]}
RESULT: PASS — unchanged, still authenticates.

=== AC3: employee happy path ===
Read-only DB check: `vendor_employees` table has 0 rows in dev DB (no seeded employee auth_token exists) -> live HTTP repro not possible for this AC.
Fallback per ticket's sanctioned evidence path: phpunit.
$ vendor/bin/phpunit --filter VendorGuardSeedingTest --testdox
 Owner token seeds vendor guard and store id ................ PASS
 Employee token seeds both guards and store id ............... PASS
 Missing vendor type header is rejected ....................... PASS
 Invalid owner token is rejected and arms nothing ............. PASS
 Unknown vendor type fails closed and arms nothing ............ PASS
Tests: 5, Assertions: 21 — all green.
RESULT: PASS (via phpunit, employee path unchanged and still authenticates + arms both guards).

=== Falsifiability check (QA-independent re-verification) ===
Temporarily reverted VendorTokenIsValid.php else-branch to pre-fix `$ok();` (local, not committed),
re-ran test_unknown_vendor_type_fails_closed_and_arms_nothing:
  FAIL — "unknown vendorType must NOT reach the protected route ($next) / Failed asserting that true is false."
Restored fix, re-ran full VendorGuardSeedingTest suite -> 5/5 PASS again.
Confirms the test is a real, falsifiable proof of the fix (not a tautology).

=== Regression sweep ===
1) Empty vendorType header, valid bearer -> 403 {"errors":[{"code":"vendor_type","message":"Vendor type required"}]} — unchanged pre-login gate.
2) No bearer at all -> 401 {"errors":[{"code":"auth-001","message":"Unauthorized."}]} — unchanged.
3) Owner happy path -> 200 full profile payload — unchanged (see AC2).
4) Full `Security` phpunit testsuite (452 tests / 2211 assertions) -> all green, no regressions.

=== Logs-first check ===
storage/logs/laravel.log during the live curl session: no [ERR]/[FAIL] lines (checked before and after).
[FAIL] lines present in the log are from the phpunit "testing" channel's own deliberate failure-path
fixtures (SQL-secret-leak test, product-rating 500 test, store-not-found review tests) — unrelated to
this route/middleware, pre-existing test behavior, not a regression.
